Release 2 renamed `title`; release 3 deleted its lines (`@oldest 2`)
while a database (a teammate's) was still at release 1. It is refused, the
ledger saying why, never migrated with its values lost. Putting release
2's lines back, it goes through.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'soup');
PRAGMA user_version = 1;

== after
-- @release 3
-- @oldest 2
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== after
-- @release 3
-- @drop 2 column dish title
-- @from 2 column dish name = title
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== plan
-- after 1
-- after 2
roux: migrating test.db, 4 steps
  table `dish`: aside, to make it anew
    ALTER TABLE "dish" RENAME TO "roux_old_dish"
  table `dish`: as schema.sql makes it
    CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT
  table `dish`: its rows, by id, name = title
    INSERT INTO "dish" ("id", "name") SELECT "id", (
    title
    ) FROM "roux_old_dish"
  table `dish`: the old one
    DROP TABLE "roux_old_dish"
migrated from release 1

== error
-- after 1
the database is at release 1, before `-- @oldest 2`: the @drop and @from lines it needs were deleted. Open it first with an executable of a release that still had them, or put them back.

== query
SELECT id, name FROM dish

== rows
1 | soup
